    "Since the GDP definition is still being confirmed internally, which of these readings should I implement for now: (A) GDP equals the total value of the four goods produced domestically at world-market prices, (B) GDP equals the value of domestic production minus the value of imported goods used, or (C) GDP equals the value of final goods only (excluding intermediate inputs)?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response presents a single multiple-choice question asking the user to select one specific definition from three options. Although it lists three alternatives, it requires a single policy choice, making it one semantically independent question."
}

